{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-grafana-2026-12704",
  "summary": "SAML assertion replay via skipped InResponseTo validation",
  "details": "When SAML IdP-initiated login is enabled in Grafana Enterprise, the SAML library skips validation of the InResponseTo field on all SAML responses, including SP-initiated logins. This removes anti-replay protection, allowing an attacker who obtains a valid signed SAML assertion to replay it and gain a session as the victim user. Only instances with the allow_idp_initiated SAML setting enabled are affected; this setting is off by default and Grafana OSS is not affected.",
